cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tissue Weather in a course or in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Tissue Weather"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based 3D teaching interactive for tissue engineering. A generic simulation engine
  (voxel grid, matrix species, diffusible fields, cell agents, fiber orientation tensor) is
  driven by plug-in tissue definitions; students turn environmental "weather" dials and watch
  the extracellular matrix condense, align, mature, scar or evaporate through dynamic
  reciprocity. Ships with fibrous connective tissue and cartilage in a degrading hydrogel,
  a lesson plan, headless scenario tools and a Blender importer for cinematic renders.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peponis
    given-names: John
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
